<title>USA: TABLE-Int'l  Business Machines sells debt.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Int'l  Business Machines sells debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>International Business Machines Corp (IBM) issued $1.0 billion in a two-tranche debt deal on Wednesday, according to lead manager Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter, Discover &amp; Co.</p>
<p>IBM makes mainframe computers, PC's, LAN products, software and peripherals.</p>
<p>BORROWER INTERNATIONAL BUSINESS MACHINES CORP</p>
<p>AMT $500 MLN	 COUPON 6.45 PCT   MATURITY 8/1/2007</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.694  FIRST PAY DATE 2/1/1998</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A1    YIELD  6.492 PCT  PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P SINGLE-A  SPREAD +44 BPS    CALLABLE  NO</p>
